---
import InteriorLayout from "../layouts/InteriorLayout.astro";
import TextLink from "../components/ui/TextLink.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/url";
import heroImg from "../assets/gallery/fan-veg.webp";
---

<InteriorLayout
  title="What We Do"
  description="Four ways the Endangered Habitats League protects Southern California's wild places: saving nature, strategic planning, collaboration, and land trust stewardship."
  eyebrow="What We Do"
  heading="Four ways we protect the region"
  heroImage={heroImg}
  intro="Dedicated to the protection of the diverse ecosystems of Southern California — and to sensitive, sustainable land use for the benefit of all the region's inhabitants."
>
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-12 px-5 pb-16 tablet:gap-16 tablet:px-14">
    <section id="saving-nature">
      <h2 class="text-h2 text-text-primary">Saving Nature</h2>
      <p class="text-lede mt-3 max-w-[720px] text-text-quote">
        EHL identifies and safeguards our most critical lands.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[720px] text-[15px] leading-[1.6] text-text-secondary">
        From majestic oak woodlands and scenic meadows, to gentle hillsides
        of coastal sage scrub, to the life sustaining waters of streams and
        wetlands, we advocate for the preservation of natural habitats in
        San Diego, Orange, Riverside, Los Angeles and San Bernardino
        Counties and related ecological regions.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[720px] text-[15px] leading-[1.6] text-text-secondary">
        EHL gives voice to the plants and animals for whom it is our
        privilege and responsibility to speak. This region is one of the
        world's most biologically diverse, and many of our plant and animal
        species are threatened with extinction. As Southern California's
        only regional conservation organization, EHL has led the way in
        establishing an unprecedented, interconnected system of nature
        reserves. However, there is much more work to do. By focusing on
        science-based priorities, and using the Endangered Species Act as
        leverage, we continue the monumental work of preserving our natural
        heritage for future generations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="strategic-planning">
      <h2 class="text-h2 text-text-primary">Strategic Planning</h2>
      <p class="text-lede mt-3 max-w-[720px] text-text-quote">
        EHL works to establish healthy co-existence between people and
        nature by integrating comprehensive and sustainable land use with
        permanent resource protection.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[720px] text-[15px] leading-[1.6] text-text-secondary">
        Boasting one of the world's most desirable climates as well as
        beautiful natural landscapes, Southern California's metropolitan
        region draws a constant influx of new businesses and residents. In
        response, EHL participates in regional planning to curtail sprawl
        and preserve intact natural landscapes. We actively support the
        revitalization of urban areas and the development of vibrant
        community centers with effective mobility and affordable housing.
        Through our continued participation in planning efforts, we aim to
        achieve the highest quality of life possible for all the region's
        inhabitants.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="collaboration">
      <h2 class="text-h2 text-text-primary">Collaboration</h2>
      <p class="text-lede mt-3 max-w-[720px] text-text-quote">
        EHL bases its environmental advocacy on collaboration.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[720px] text-[15px] leading-[1.6] text-text-secondary">
        Together with communities, businesses, landowners, and government
        agencies, we develop solutions that serve all stakeholders while
        preserving nature. Our integrity and results-oriented methodology
        have garnered respect and credibility among a broad spectrum of
        groups and agencies. These relationships continue to lead to ever
        greater opportunities for conservation.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[720px] text-[15px] leading-[1.6] text-text-secondary">
        As a team of seasoned professionals, we at EHL apply the highest
        standards to all aspects of our work. We drive the implementation
        of state-of-the-art management and monitoring practices for the
        stewardship of preserve lands. We use sound science and careful
        research to produce the most effective environmental advocacy and
        best conservation practices. When all other means have been
        exhausted, we take legal measures to protect our natural heritage.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="land-trust">
      <h2 class="text-h2 text-text-primary">Land Trust</h2>
      <p class="text-lede mt-3 max-w-[720px] text-text-quote">
        The Endangered Habitats Conservancy (EHC) is a separate nonprofit
        land trust organization that works closely with EHL to help
        conserve the remaining natural wildlands of Southern California.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[720px] text-[15px] leading-[1.6] text-text-secondary">
        EHC acquires, manages, monitors and maintains land in Southern
        California for habitat protection and restoration, agricultural
        preservation, and other conservation purposes, and currently
        manages approximately 10,000 acres of conserved open space. It
        plays a critical role in assembling our preserve systems through
        strategic land acquisitions, and leads the way with high quality
        management and monitoring practices for the stewardship of
        preserve lands.
      </p>
      <TextLink href={withBase("/land-trust/")} tone="on-paper" class="mt-4">
        Learn more about EHC
      </TextLink>
    </section>
  </div>
</InteriorLayout>
